{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-87586171c764dbb7", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Contrastive Flow Matching\narXiv: 2506.05350\nAuthors: George Stoica, Vivek Ramanujan, Xiang Fan, Ali Farhadi, Ranjay Krishna, Judy Hoffman\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduces Contrastive Flow Matching, an extension to the flow matching objective that explicitly enforces uniqueness across conditional flows to enhance condition separation.\n  2. Adds a contrastive regularization term that maximizes dissimilarities between predicted flows from arbitrary sample pairs within a training batch.\n  3. Demonstrates up to 9x faster training speed compared to standard flow matching.\n  4. Achieves equivalent or superior image quality with up to 5x fewer denoising steps during inference.\n  5. Lowers Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) by up to 8.9 points on class-conditional and text-to-image benchmarks.\n  6. Shows complementary benefits when combined with Representation Alignment (REPA) for further performance improvements.\n  7. Introduces a modified classifier-free guidance equation to resolve conflicts and successfully stack the benefits of both methods.\n===SEP===\n===SEP===\n===SEP===", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "fb8d177a-be04-450b-a6f6-fcc4f4ffda35", "uuid": "428148d6-732a-4ea1-bb06-3a45b05b2962", "timestamp": "2026-08-07T08:26:06.244Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Contrastive Flow Matching\narXiv: 2506.05350\nAuthors: George Stoica, Vivek Ramanujan, Xiang Fan, Ali Farhadi, Ranjay Krishna, Judy Hoffman\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduces Contrastive Flow Matching, an extension to the flow matching objective that explicitly enforces uniqueness across conditional flows to enhance condition separation.\n  2. Adds a contrastive regularization term that maximizes dissimilarities between predicted flows from arbitrary sample pairs within a training batch.\n  3. Demonstrates up to 9x faster training speed compared to standard flow matching.\n  4. Achieves equivalent or superior image quality with up to 5x fewer denoising steps during inference.\n  5. Lowers Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) by up to 8.9 points on class-conditional and text-to-image benchmarks.\n  6. Shows complementary benefits when combined with Representation Alignment (REPA) for further performance improvements.\n  7. Introduces a modified classifier-free guidance equation to resolve conflicts and successfully stack the benefits of both methods.\n===SEP===\n===SEP===\n===SEP===", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
